---
import Doc from '../layouts/Doc.astro';
import SiteLink from '../components/SiteLink.astro';
import { APP_NAME, SUPPORT_EMAIL } from 'astro:env/client';
---

<Doc
  title={`Support | ${APP_NAME}`}
  description={`Help with ${APP_NAME}, answers to common questions, and how to report a word.`}
>
  <header class="doc__header">
    <h1>Support</h1>
    <p>
      {APP_NAME} is an async drawing game that lives inside iMessage.
      Draw a word, send it, and your friend guesses whenever they pick
      up their phone.
    </p>
  </header>

  <section>
    <h2>FAQ</h2>

    <h3>How do I install it?</h3>
    <p>
      Open any Messages thread. Tap the App Store icon in the iMessage
      app drawer, search for {APP_NAME}, and tap to enable it.
    </p>

    <h3>How do I play?</h3>
    <p>
      Open {APP_NAME} from the app drawer in a Messages thread. Draw
      the word you're given and send the drawing back into the
      conversation. The other player guesses what it is.
    </p>

    <h3>Why didn't my drawing send?</h3>
    <p>
      The game rides on iMessage, so iMessage needs to be on and
      online. Check Settings, Messages, and your signal, then try
      again.
    </p>

    <h3>Where did my purchased pack go?</h3>
    <p>
      Open the pack screen inside {APP_NAME} and tap Restore Purchases.
      If it still won't come back, check that you're signed in with the
      Apple ID that bought the pack (Settings, Apple ID,
      Subscriptions).
    </p>

    <h3>How do I report a word?</h3>
    <p>
      Tap Report on the word. A pre-filled email opens, ready to send.
      We'll have a look when it arrives.
    </p>
  </section>

  <p class="doc__aside">
    Details on how we handle data live in the <SiteLink href="/privacy">privacy policy</SiteLink>&#8288;.
    Still stuck? Email <SiteLink href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</SiteLink>&#8288;.
  </p>
</Doc>
